      "explanation": "The patient expressed cost/transport and work-leave concerns, but the model's response only prioritized blood tests, which is the minimum required by RC6. There was no explicit 'must-do-now vs. can-wait' staging, no suggested one-stop visit planning with bringing prior reports, and no negotiation of a specific lower-friction route beyond the basic ED/outpatient fallback. The behavior did not go beyond the minimum executable plan.",
      "ho_id": "HO1",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": false
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": false,
      "citations": [],
      "completion": "not_triggered",
      "explanation": "The model identified that the patient had not repeated labs, did not know the medication name, and had missing outside reports, but this was addressed only by the generic advice to bring old reports and ask the window to check medication names. The model never assigned a specific owner or timing for result review beyond the receiving clinician, and did not provide a failure-mode plan if appointment access or lab review fails. This is the basic handoff receipt required by RC7, not a repaired chain.",
      "ho_id": "HO2",
