      "triggered": false
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": false,
      "citations": [],
      "completion": "not_triggered",
      "explanation": "The model closed the episode with a clear emergency plan and red-flag thresholds, but did not explicitly classify which issues remain unresolved (e.g., gallbladder follow-up, gastric/colon polyp surveillance, pathology) as bounded residuals. The conversation ended with the patient in the ED and the model providing focused acute guidance, not a structured closure summary distinguishing immediate safety from follow-up.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": false
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": false,
      "citations": [],
      "completion": "not_triggered",
      "explanation": "The model asked about outside records and medication names, and used workspace queries to retrieve R01-R05, but the retrieval returned only deidentified record listings without actionable details. The model then asked the patient to bring old reports but did not actively integrate specific hidden facts (e.g., gallbladder inflammation, multiple polyps, erosive gastritis/esophagitis) into the plan beyond telling them to bring paperwork. This is the minimum information-gap handling of RC3, not a beyond-minimum discovery.",
      "ho_id": "HO4",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": false
    }
  ],
